   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to establishing the New York\nAsian American and Pacific Islander commission and providing for its duties;\nto amend a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the executive law relating to\nestablishing the New York Asian American and Pacific Islander commission, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 1051-A and A. 3301-A, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof; and to repeal section 295-a of the executive law\nrelating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S8023",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8023-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §295-a, add §94-d, Exec L; amd §2, Chap of 2023 (as proposed in S.1051-A & A.3301-A)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8023\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to establishing the New\nYork Asian American and Pacific Islander commission and providing for\nits duties; to amend a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the execu-\ntive law relating to establishing the New York Asian American and Pacif-\nic Islander commission, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n1051-A and A.  3301-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and to\nrepeal section 295-a of the executive law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2023,\nc.639, to move the New York Asian American and Pacific Islander commis-\nsion from existing under the Division of Human Rights to the Department\nof State, lowering its membership to thirteen members, making its find-\nings recommendations, and setting a five year sunset.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one repeals Section 295-a of the Executive Law, which estab-\nlished a New York Asian American and Pacific Islander commission under\nthe Division of Human Rights.\n\nSection 2 creates a new section 94-d of the Executive Law to establish a\nNew York Asian American and Pacific islander commission under the\nDepartment of State. This thirteen-member commission, with seven\nappointees from the Governor and six from the Legislature will make\nrecommendations on policies to improve the well-being of Asian Americans\nand Pacific Islanders, make these communities aware of available state\nprograms and resources, and ways to increase public awareness of Asian\nAmerican and Pacific Islander culture and concerns. This commission\nshall report annually to the Governor and the Legislature.\n\nSection 3 amends the effective date of Chapter 639 to set a five-year\nsunset. Section 4 sets the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 636 of the Laws of 2023. S.1051-A and\nA.3301-A both passed the Senate and Assembly in June 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that sections\none and two of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the\nsame manner as a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the executive law\nrelating to establishing the New York Asian American and Pacific Islan-\nder commission, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.1051-A and A.\n3301-A, takes effect.\n",
